State-Store

State with undo, redo and watchers.

A store holds one value and is the place a program asks for the current
one. It is meant for values from HAMT, where keeping an old version costs
almost nothing, so that undo is a matter of pointing at the version before.

Requires a C compiler, perl 5.10 or later, and HAMT.


INSTALLATION

To install this module, run the following commands:

	perl Makefile.PL
	make
	make test
	make install

SUPPORT AND DOCUMENTATION

After installing, you can find documentation for this module with the
perldoc command.

    perldoc State::Store

You can also look for information at:

    RT, CPAN's request tracker (report bugs here)
        https://rt.cpan.org/NoAuth/Bugs.html?Dist=State-Store

    Search CPAN
        https://metacpan.org/release/State-Store


